      "answerParts": [
        {
          "partIndex": 0,
          "text": "### Deceleration and Supersonic Retropropulsion\n* A reusable rocket first-stage booster relies on rocket fuel to decelerate during entry and landing because atmospheric drag alone is insufficient to protect the vehicle and ensure a controlled descent.\n* Firing rocket engines against the direction of travel\u00e2\u20ac\u201da process known as retropropulsion\u00e2\u20ac\u201dallows the vehicle to shed hypersonic and supersonic velocities, manage thermal loads, and target a specific touchdown location.\n* Deceleration under engine power is the only entry, descent, and landing technology that is intrinsically scalable across a wide range of massive vehicles to enable safe landings on both Earth and airless"
        }
      ],
